    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the Owner schema (the OwnerDto is generated from this spec), documenting the fixed table.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/Localities.java`** \u2014 Added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneFor(Owner)` method that reuses the existing `localityFor(owner)` region derivation, returning the IANA name (or `null` for `UNKNOWN`/unmapped regions, so the field is simply absent).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `timezone` calling `Localities.timezoneFor(owner)`, alongside the existing `locality` mapping.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` test (Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
